# EVAL-ONLY witness W-R23 (never in a prompt or training file).
# Three-stage op-amp with active-feedback frequency compensation (AFFC, Lee & Mok),
# transcribed from AnalogGym Amplifier/spice_netlist/HoiLee_AFFC_Pin_3 (mapping table in
# witnesses/README.md). AnalogGym device xmK -> name below; nets kept (lower-cased).
# Stage 1: PMOS-input folded cascode (pair M9a/M9b, tail M4, NMOS sinks M20a/M20b,
#   NMOS cascodes M16a/M16b, PMOS mirror load M0d/M0e) -> net050.
# Stage 2 (non-inverting): PMOS M11 (gate net050) into the NMOS diode M22a, mirrored by
#   M22b onto net049 against the PMOS source M0f.
# Stage 3: NMOS M25 (gate net049) + feedforward PMOS M12 (gate net050) -> VOUT.
# Compensation: Miller C0 (net049 -> VOUT); active feedback: C1 (VOUT -> net1) into the
#   common-gate NMOS M60b (gate vb3) that feeds net050; M59a/M59b + M60a + M18c return
#   M60b's DC current to net050.
# Bias: AnalogGym's ideal sink I0 out of the PMOS diode net013 is replaced by our one
#   IREF: NMOS diode MB1a + 1:1 mirror MB1b pulling IREF out of net013 (I0 == IREF).
#   PMOS mirrors M0b -> vb4, M0c -> vb3; vb3 diode M15; vb4 = cascoded diode M18b/M18a.
#   AnalogGym's dummy branch dm_1 (xm2, xm14, xm19) is dropped.
NMOS MB1a IREF IREF VSS
NMOS MB1b net013 IREF VSS
PMOS M0a net013 net013 VDD
PMOS M0b vb4 net013 VDD
PMOS M0c vb3 net013 VDD
PMOS M0d voutn voutn VDD
PMOS M0e net050 voutn VDD
PMOS M0f net049 net013 VDD
PMOS M4 net31 net013 VDD
PMOS M9a dm_2 VINN net31 net31
PMOS M9b net063 VINP net31 net31
NMOS M20a dm_2 vb4 VSS
NMOS M20b net063 vb4 VSS
NMOS M16a voutn vb3 dm_2
NMOS M16b net050 vb3 net063
NMOS M15 vb3 vb3 VSS
NMOS M18b vb4 vb3 net54
NMOS M18a net54 vb4 VSS
PMOS M11 net043 net050 VDD
NMOS M22a net043 net043 VSS
NMOS M22b net049 net043 VSS
NMOS M25 VOUT net049 VSS
PMOS M12 VOUT net050 VDD
PMOS M59a net2 net2 VDD
PMOS M59b net050 net2 VDD
NMOS M60a net2 vb3 net3
NMOS M60b net050 vb3 net1
NMOS M18c net3 vb4 VSS
NMOS M18d net1 vb4 VSS
C C0 net049 VOUT
C C1 VOUT net1
